From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 07:59:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: give the primary output a 5 ms nominal latency

The primary module reports a nominal latency of 85 ms, which gives its
PCM streams a 4096-frame buffer at 48 kHz. AudioFlinger creates a fast
mixer only for an output whose HAL buffer is shorter than its 20 ms
normal sink, so the primary output has none: every fast track request
is refused, AAudio low-latency streams fall back to the normal mixer,
and a tap in a game is heard about a quarter of a second later.

Report 5 ms for the output, which rounds to a 256-frame buffer: the
output gets a fast mixer and grants fast tracks. The product sizes the
ALSA ring as four periods of one buffer each, a 1024-frame output ring.

Report 20 ms for the input, a 1024-frame buffer, which keeps the
input's ALSA ring of four 1024-frame periods at every rate; a period
of a whole 4096-frame buffer would exceed the Virtio sound driver's
largest. MMAP streams keep 10 ms.
---
 audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp | 13 ++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
index 9e4e9e7575fff49970903c7d9a5312c76ead6153..6e2f2e9e9f16e1933bf4b6dc74a42d2fb396b95f 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/ModulePrimary.cpp
@@ -151,11 +151,14 @@ ndk::ScopedAStatus ModulePrimary::createMmapBuffer(const AudioPortConfig& portCo
 
 int32_t ModulePrimary::getNominalLatencyMs(const AudioPortConfig& portConfig) {
     static constexpr int32_t kLowLatencyMs = 10;
-    // 85 ms is chosen considering 4096 frames @ 48 kHz. This is the value which allows
-    // the virtual Android device implementation to pass CTS. Hardware implementations
-    // should have significantly lower latency.
-    static constexpr int32_t kStandardLatencyMs = 85;
-    return hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value()) ? kLowLatencyMs : kStandardLatencyMs;
+    // The product's ALSA ring holds four periods of one buffer each. 5 ms is 256 frames
+    // @ 48 kHz once rounded up to a power of two: AudioFlinger gives an output whose buffer
+    // is shorter than its 20 ms normal sink a fast mixer, and only then grants fast tracks.
+    static constexpr int32_t kOutputLatencyMs = 5;
+    // 20 ms is 1024 frames @ 48 kHz, which keeps the input's 1024-frame periods.
+    static constexpr int32_t kInputLatencyMs = 20;
+    if (hasMmapFlag(portConfig.flags.value())) return kLowLatencyMs;
+    return portConfig.flags->getTag() == AudioIoFlags::input ? kInputLatencyMs : kOutputLatencyMs;
 }
 
 ndk::ScopedAStatus ModulePrimary::getFlushFromFrameSupport(const AudioPortConfig& in_config,
